C++ host tests
==============

Run by PlatformIO's native env (see platformio.ini):

    pio test -e native                    all suites
    pio test -e native -f test_planner    lib/planner, and checkBezier on real records
    pio test -e native -f test_config     the Pico's config decoder

    ./.pio/build/native/program.exe -s    assertion counts; pio hides them

Generated data
--------------

test/data/bezier_records.txt is the BEZIER records the web pipeline makes from
fish.svg, written as wire bytes. It is tracked. Its generator is
web/test/port/cppRefBezier.test.ts; regenerate it when load, clean, annotate or
the packet format changes:

    cd web && GEN_CPP_REF=1 npx vitest run test/port

Without GEN_CPP_REF=1 the generator skips, so it costs nothing in a normal
vitest run.

Check these files with is_open(), never good(): a default-constructed
std::ifstream has no error flags set, so good() returns true for a stream that
was never opened.

Layout
------

    main.cpp           doctest runner. In the test_dir ROOT, which PlatformIO
                       shares into every suite.
    support/bits.h     openRef: finds a file in test/data
    data/              generated; see above
    test_planner/      lib/planner
    test_config/       config decode
